WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.412
Why this module?

2
00:00:01.412 --> 00:00:05.572
Every other lab in this path starts
from an account that already exists:

3
00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:10.351
a user account used as a service, a standalone
managed service account, or a secret.

4
00:00:10.351 --> 00:00:14.288
You move its S P Ns, run in
parallel, then disable it.

5
00:00:14.288 --> 00:00:16.225
This module starts from nothing.

6
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:21.604
First the forest gets what every G
M S A needs, once: a K D S root key,

7
00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:27.088
the O Us, a group that may create G M
S As, and the pipeline's own G M S A.

8
00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:30.625
Then a new application gets
its G M S A from the first day,

9
00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:34.478
by the managed service account
standard, with no S P N to move,

10
00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:37.387
no parallel run and no
old account to disable.

11
00:00:37.387 --> 00:00:40.873
That's why it comes before
Module 8: Module 8 converts the

12
00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:44.900
accounts that already exist, into
the forest this module sets up.
